  "query_preview": "/Tuesday through Saturday/...\nIssued 240 AM MST SAT NOV 28 2026\nRain and mountain snow will slowly decrease on Tuesday as an\nupper level trough axis swings through the forecast area, \nultimately shunting the moisture toward the east. Temperatures \nwill be a few degrees cooler Tuesday night into Wednesday in the\nwake of the trough. A flattened upper ridge will swiftly \ndevelop over the region later Wednesday, allowing drier weather \nto prevail through Thursday or Friday. Models suggest a cooler, \nshowery trough will approach the area Saturday, increasing \nprecipitation chances and lowering temperatures by several \ndegrees over next weekend.",
